  https://github.com/FoxIO-LLC/ja4/blob/main/LICENSE-JA4
  https://github.com/lum8rjack/caddy-ja4h/blob/main/NOTICE

If you deploy the Caddy image built by caddy/Dockerfile, or redistribute it, the
FoxIO terms apply to you. Running this honeypot as personal or academic research
is within them. Building a commercial product on the fingerprints it collects is
not, absent a licence.

To avoid the dependency entirely, remove the two `--with` lines from
caddy/Dockerfile and use a stock Caddy image. The service degrades gracefully:
`ja4` and `ja4h` are recorded as empty strings and nothing else changes.

